  "_readme": "HDA property names for Synora. `columns` are the core fields every record needs; `fields` are the extended HDA mapping (tier search: added to the searchable text; tier detail: stored and shown in the record panel only; person: a name, never searchable or sent to the AI). Linked records are read by name (X.Description); when HDA rejects an expression the sync drops it, or uses `fallback` (the raw ID), and logs it. Fields of ticket types Synora never indexes (SEC*, EL13*, EL144*, EL26*), attachments and internal flags are left out on purpose. Run npm run hda:discover to check the mapping against HDA.",
